!   unit-03-time.allspeak — tests `ConvertTimeToInt`, mirrored verbatim from
!   controller.allspeak:1339.
!
!   Part of the RBR validation of the new testing vocabulary.
!
!   The subroutine returns milliseconds since midnight PLUS `today`, so an
!   absolute result is wall-clock dependent. Differences between two times of
!   the same day are normally constant — 08:30 - 07:00 is 1.5 hours = 5400000 ms
!   — but a span that crosses a daylight-saving change is an hour longer or
!   shorter in real time, and the full-day case asserts exactly that.
!
!   NOTE: this mirrors the subroutine as it stands today; it is not linked to
!   the live code. Keep in sync with controller.allspeak if the conversion changes.

    script Unit03Time

    variable Time
    variable I
    variable T
    variable SevenAM
    variable Midnight
    variable EightThirty
    variable HourNow
    variable MinuteNow
    variable H
    variable M

    go to RunTests

!! Convert "HH:MM" to milliseconds since local midnight, then add `today`. Both padded (`08:30`) and non-padded (`8:30`) hours parse. A daylight-saving day is not 24 hours long, so the candidate is corrected to its own local wall clock (mirrors controller.allspeak).

ConvertTimeToInt:
    put `` cat Time into Time
    put the index of `:` in Time into I
    put the value of left I of Time into T
    multiply T by 60
    increment I
    put the value of from I of Time into Time
    add Time to T
    multiply T by 60000 giving Time
    add today to Time
    put the hour of Time into I
    multiply I by 60
    add the minute of Time to I
    take I from T
    if T is greater than 720 take 1440 from T
    else if T is less than -720 add 1440 to T
    multiply T by 60000
    add T to Time
    return
!! @hash a147d156
!!!

RunTests:

!! 07:00 to 08:30 is exactly 90 minutes = 5400000 ms.

    test `90-minute span`
        put `07:00` into Time
        gosub to ConvertTimeToInt
        put Time into SevenAM
        put `08:30` into Time
        gosub to ConvertTimeToInt
        take SevenAM from Time
        check that Time is 5400000
    end test
!! @hash 5d19683b
!!!

!! 00:00 to 23:59 is normally 1439 minutes = 86340000 ms; a spring-forward day is an hour shorter and a fall-back day an hour longer.

    test `full-day span is 23, 24 or 25 hours`
        put `00:00` into Time
        gosub to ConvertTimeToInt
        put Time into Midnight
        put `23:59` into Time
        gosub to ConvertTimeToInt
        take Midnight from Time
        check that Time is 86340000 or Time is 89940000 or Time is 82740000
    end test
!! @hash 536a5d22
!!!

!! A non-padded hour (`8:30`) parses identically to `08:30` — their difference is zero.

    test `non-padded hour parses identically`
        put `08:30` into Time
        gosub to ConvertTimeToInt
        put Time into EightThirty
        put `8:30` into Time
        gosub to ConvertTimeToInt
        take EightThirty from Time
        check that Time is 0
    end test
!! @hash f75bc824
!!!

!! The conversion must land on the wall-clock time it was handed, whatever the date — the guard that was missing on 2026-10-25, when an 08:00 period began at 07:00 because the conversion assumed a fixed offset from local midnight.

    test `conversion lands on the wall clock it was given`
        put the hour into HourNow
        put the minute into MinuteNow
        put `` cat HourNow cat `:` cat MinuteNow into Time
        gosub to ConvertTimeToInt
        put the hour of Time into H
        put the minute of Time into M
        check that H is HourNow and M is MinuteNow
    end test
!! @hash 66339491
!!!

    exit
!! @hash b43c908e
!!!
